# Cloudflare Pages picks this file up automatically from the deployed
# output root (Vite copies public/ into dist/ at build time) and applies
# these headers to every response. Django's own CSP (hms/middleware.py)
# only covers pages Django serves - the admin panel and DRF's browsable
# API. This SPA is a separate static deployment and needs its own.
#
# TODO before deploying: replace <API_ORIGIN> below with the real deployed
# API origin (e.g. https://hms-api.up.railway.app) - a static file can't
# read VITE_API_BASE_URL at request time, so this has to be kept in sync
# by hand. Getting it wrong fails closed: the SPA simply can't reach the
# API, not a silent security hole - worth checking once, at deploy time.
#
# Verified against the real dist/ build in a browser (see
# notes/CSP_2026-09-09.md): zero console violations with no unsafe-inline
# anywhere - this app has no dangerouslySetInnerHTML/innerHTML/eval, so a
# fully strict policy works as-is, not just in theory.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; connect-src 'self' https://hms-dv4m.onrender.com; frame-ancestors 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'

  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
